WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.080
Just follow along step by step.

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.720
Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12 tablets each and a measured

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:10.960
container.

5
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.760
Start your first dose between 6 and 7 PM the night before your procedure.

6
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.160
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets.

7
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.040
Fill the provided container with 16 ounces of water up to the fill line.

8
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.920
Swallow one tablet every 2 minutes with a sip of water, finishing all 12

9
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:28.640
tablets over

10
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.560
about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at a steady pace.

11
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.910
About 1 hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

12
00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:38.560
of water and

13
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:43.440
drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes. Then, about 30 minutes after

14
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.000
finishing that

15
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.830
container, fill it one more time with 16 ounces of water and drink the entire

16
00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.120
amount over 30 minutes.

17
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.120
That completes your first dose.

18
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:57.070
7 hours prior to your procedure, repeat the exact same three steps using

19
00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:57.840
your second bottle

20
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.800
of 12 tablets. One tablet every 2 minutes with water, then 16 ounces of water

21
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.760
one hour later,

22
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.320
then 16 ounces of water 30 minutes after that.

23
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.970
This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep solution as

24
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:11.520
directed,

25
00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.240
even if you're already passing clear liquid. I know it can feel like enough,

26
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.100
but finishing the entire dose is what gives us the clearest view during your

27
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:20.640
procedure.

28
00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.840
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule, and neither

29
00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:26.960
of us wants that.

30
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.120
Between doses, keep drinking clear liquids to stay hydrated.

31
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.000
It will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

32
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.800
Do not drink anything at all within 4 hours of your procedure,

33
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.000
including water, unless it is a small sip to take a medication.

34
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.640
Your procedure may be canceled or rescheduled if this is not followed.

35
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:49.920
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

36
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.600
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

37
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.930
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

38
00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:00.480
hydrated.

39
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:05.660
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

40
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.800
to help.
